        ["Under which iontophoresis electrode is an alkaline skin reaction MOST likely to develop?",["The cathode (negative electrode)","The anode (positive electrode)","Both electrodes equally","Neither, since DC has no effect"],"Direct current causes an alkaline reaction under the cathode and an acidic reaction under the anode, so skin under both should be checked, with particular attention to the cathode."]
